## Context

Orchestration child of tracker `0613`. This ticket is the conjunction over the
R15 acceptance audit performed 2026-09-04. It owns no implementation itself:
each independently reviewable defect is a child below, and this tracker closes
only after all children close and their resulting assertions have been run
against zoteus.

R15 has two scales. The item scale requires trashing an item to remove its text
from every store and queue. The install scale requires a complete declaration,
model-cache containment, and removal of all declared state after uninstall. The
current harness omits the item scale entirely and has false-green paths in each
install-scale assertion: an arena-bounded/install-only residue sweep, uninstall
without materialized-state proof and with file-only survivor accounting, model
placement without proof of a download, and fail-controls accepted when any
unrelated fixture happens to make an assertion red. README then claims coverage
that does not exist.

## Work

Coordinate children 0654-0659. Merge order is unconstrained among the five
harness children; 0659 follows them because public coverage must be read from
the resulting assertions and real artifact, never computed in advance. When a
child lands, rebase/re-measure the remaining live lanes under the repository's
merge-authority rules.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] children 0654-0659 are closed with their own exit criteria met
- [ ] every R15 MUST clause maps to a registered assertion with a discriminating
      red control
- [ ] a real zoteus run records an honest verdict for every R15 assertion
- [ ] tracker 0613 records every R15 clause and its measured verdict
- [ ] `make check` passes

## Children

| child | scope |
|---|---|
| 0654 | trash-time item deletion through every store and queue |
| 0655 | residue inventory reach across lifecycle surfaces and filesystem escapes |
| 0656 | uninstall materialization precondition and complete survivor accounting |
| 0657 | evidence that a model download occurred before cache placement is graded |
| 0658 | assertion-specific fail-controls enforced by the normal gate |
| 0659 | README and tracker coverage map corrected from the completed harness |
